---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="State of Stick Golf — A Connected Future for Golf" description="A simple, tap-connected system for golfers, golf courses, clubhouses, and leagues." eyebrow="STATE OF STICK / GOLF PRODUCT BRIEF" image="/art/golf-fairway-hero.png">
  <style is:global>
    .brief-page { --brief-green:#173b2c; --brief-ink:#172019; --brief-paper:#f5f1e7; --brief-copper:#c66b3d; --brief-muted:#53605a; background:var(--brief-paper); color:var(--brief-ink); }
    .brief-page h1,.brief-page h2,.brief-page h3,.brief-page p { max-width:none; }
    .brief-hero { padding:0 0 88px; background:radial-gradient(circle at 78% 18%,rgba(74,104,78,.24),transparent 31%),var(--brief-ink); color:#fffdf7; }
    .brief-shell { width:min(1120px,calc(100% - 44px)); margin:0 auto; }
    .brief-kicker { color:#d99a74; font:700 12px 'DM Mono',monospace; letter-spacing:.14em; }
    .brief-lockup { display:none; }
    .brief-lockup img { width:68px; height:68px; padding:0; background:#fffdf7; border-radius:50%; object-fit:cover; }
    .brief-lockup strong { display:block; color:#fffdf7; font-size:18px; letter-spacing:.02em; }
    .brief-lockup span { display:block; margin-top:5px; color:#bdc5bd; font:11px 'DM Mono',monospace; letter-spacing:.1em; }
    .brief-hero-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.02fr .98fr; gap:68px; align-items:center; padding-top:76px; }
    .brief-hero h1 { max-width:700px; margin:18px 0 24px; color:#fffdf7; font-size:clamp(48px,6.4vw,82px); line-height:.98; letter-spacing:-.075em; }
    .brief-hero h1 em { color:#e19a70; font-style:normal; }
    .brief-hero-lead { max-width:610px; color:#d4dbd4; font-size:19px; line-height:1.55; }
    .brief-hero-image { position:relative; overflow:hidden; border:1px solid rgba(188,211,184,.3); border-radius:18px; box-shadow:0 24px 70px rgba(0,0,0,.28); }
    .brief-hero-image img { display:block; width:100%; height:510px; object-fit:cover; object-position:center; }
    .brief-image-caption { position:absolute; right:0; bottom:0; left:0; padding:20px; background:linear-gradient(transparent,rgba(11,22,15,.94)); color:#fffdf7; font-size:18px; font-weight:700; }
    .brief-demo-note { margin-top:24px; padding:14px 16px; border-left:4px solid #e19a70; background:#2a352e; color:#e4ebe3; font-size:13px; line-height:1.5; }
    .brief-section { padding:72px 0; }
    .brief-section.alt { background:#e7e4da; }
    .brief-section.dark { background:var(--brief-ink); color:#fffdf7; }
    .brief-section h2 { margin:10px 0 18px; font-size:clamp(38px,5vw,64px); line-height:1; letter-spacing:-.065em; }
    .brief-intro { max-width:700px; color:var(--brief-muted); font-size:20px; line-height:1.5; }
    .brief-stats { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr); gap:14px; margin-top:36px; }
    .brief-stat { min-height:190px; padding:24px; background:#fffdf7; border-top:5px solid var(--brief-copper); }
    .brief-stat strong { display:block; color:var(--brief-green); font-size:clamp(35px,4vw,56px); line-height:1; letter-spacing:-.07em; }
    .brief-stat span { display:block; margin-top:16px; font-size:16px; line-height:1.35; font-weight:700; }
    .brief-stat small { display:block; margin-top:10px; color:var(--brief-muted); font-size:12px; line-height:1.4; }
    .brief-source { margin-top:18px; color:#68716a; font:11px 'DM Mono',monospace; line-height:1.5; }
    .brief-source a { color:var(--brief-green); }
    .brief-two-col { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:18px; margin-top:34px; }
    .brief-card { padding:30px; background:#fffdf7; border:1px solid #d5d2c8; }
    .brief-card h3 { margin:12px 0 10px; color:var(--brief-green); font-size:28px; letter-spacing:-.045em; }
    .brief-card p { color:var(--brief-muted); font-size:17px; line-height:1.55; }
    .brief-number { color:var(--brief-copper); font:700 12px 'DM Mono',monospace; letter-spacing:.12em; }
    .brief-explainer { display:grid; grid-template-columns:.9fr 1.1fr; gap:52px; align-items:center; }
    .brief-explainer h2 { color:#fffdf7; }
    .brief-explainer > div > p { color:#d4dbd4; font-size:19px; line-height:1.55; }
    .brief-video-section { background:#202c24; color:#fffdf7; }
    .brief-video-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:.82fr 1.18fr; gap:52px; align-items:center; }
    .brief-video-copy h2 { color:#fffdf7; }
    .brief-video-copy p { color:#d4dbd4; font-size:19px; line-height:1.55; }
    .brief-video-frame { margin:0; padding:12px; background:#0d1510; border:1px solid #53635a; }
    .brief-video-frame video { display:block; width:100%; max-height:620px; object-fit:contain; background:#080c0a; }
    .brief-video-frame figcaption { padding:14px 4px 2px; color:#bdc5bd; font:11px 'DM Mono',monospace; line-height:1.5; letter-spacing:.04em; }
    .brief-video-note { margin-top:22px; padding:14px 16px; border-left:4px solid #e19a70; background:#2a352e; color:#e4ebe3; font-size:13px; line-height:1.5; }
    .brief-services { background:#e7e4da; }
    .brief-service-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr); gap:14px; margin-top:34px; }
    .brief-service-card { min-height:230px; padding:24px; background:#fffdf7; border:1px solid #d5d2c8; border-top:5px solid var(--brief-green); }
    .brief-service-card:nth-child(2),.brief-service-card:nth-child(5) { border-top-color:var(--brief-copper); }
    .brief-service-card h3 { margin:28px 0 10px; color:var(--brief-green); font-size:23px; line-height:1.05; letter-spacing:-.045em; }
    .brief-service-card p { margin:0; color:var(--brief-muted); font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; }
    .brief-service-card small { display:block; margin-top:18px; color:#7b6658; font:10px 'DM Mono',monospace; line-height:1.4; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.06em; }
    .brief-flow { display:grid; gap:10px; }
    .brief-flow-step { display:grid; grid-template-columns:58px 1fr; gap:16px; align-items:center; padding:18px; background:#fffdf7; }
    .brief-flow-step b { display:grid; place-items:center; width:46px; height:46px; border-radius:50%; background:var(--brief-copper); color:#fffdf7; font-size:20px; }
    .brief-flow-step strong { display:block; color:var(--brief-green); font-size:19px; }
    .brief-flow-step span { display:block; margin-top:4px; color:var(--brief-muted); font-size:15px; line-height:1.35; }
    .brief-proof { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:18px; margin-top:34px; }
    .brief-proof figure { margin:0; background:#fffdf7; }
    .brief-proof img { display:block; width:100%; height:260px; object-fit:cover; }
    .brief-proof figure:last-child img { object-fit:contain; background:#080c0a; }
    .brief-proof figcaption { padding:17px 20px; color:var(--brief-green); font-weight:700; }
    .brief-built { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:18px; margin-top:34px; }
    .brief-built .brief-card { border-top:5px solid var(--brief-green); }
    .brief-built .brief-card:last-child { border-top-color:var(--brief-copper); }
    .brief-money { display:grid; grid-template-columns:.95fr 1.05fr; gap:18px; margin-top:34px; }
    .brief-money .brief-card { border-top:5px solid var(--brief-green); }
    .brief-money .brief-card:last-child { border-top-color:var(--brief-copper); }
    .brief-money h3 { font-size:30px; }
    .brief-money-list { display:grid; gap:12px; margin-top:18px; }
    .brief-money-row { display:grid; grid-template-columns:112px 1fr; gap:14px; padding-top:13px; border-top:1px solid #d5d2c8; }
    .brief-money-row strong { color:var(--brief-green); font-size:16px; }
    .brief-money-row span { color:var(--brief-muted); font-size:15px; line-height:1.45; }
    .brief-economics { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr); gap:12px; margin-top:28px; }
    .brief-economics .brief-stat { min-height:0; border-top-color:var(--brief-green); }
    .brief-economics .brief-stat strong { font-size:38px; }
    .brief-economics .brief-stat span { font-size:14px; }
    .brief-economics .brief-stat small { font-family:'DM Mono',monospace; }
    .brief-offer-note { margin-top:24px; padding:18px 20px; background:#f6eadf; color:var(--brief-green); font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; }
    .brief-journey { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(5,1fr); gap:10px; margin-top:34px; }
    .brief-journey-step { position:relative; min-height:190px; padding:20px; background:#fffdf7; border-top:5px solid var(--brief-copper); }
    .brief-journey-step strong { display:block; margin:14px 0 8px; color:var(--brief-green); font-size:19px; line-height:1.1; }
    .brief-journey-step span { color:var(--brief-muted); font-size:14px; line-height:1.4; }
    .brief-workflows { display:grid; gap:14px; margin-top:34px; }
    .brief-workflow { display:grid; grid-template-columns:180px 1fr 1fr; gap:20px; padding:22px; background:#fffdf7; border-left:5px solid var(--brief-green); }
    .brief-workflow h3 { margin:0 0 8px; color:var(--brief-green); font-size:24px; }
    .brief-workflow p { margin:0; color:var(--brief-muted); font-size:15px; line-height:1.45; }
    .brief-workflow label { display:block; margin-bottom:7px; color:var(--brief-copper); font:700 11px 'DM Mono',monospace; letter-spacing:.1em; }
    .brief-partner { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:18px; margin-top:34px; }
    .brief-partner .brief-card { border-top:5px solid var(--brief-green); }
    .brief-partner .brief-card:last-child { border-top-color:var(--brief-copper); }
    .brief-checklist { display:grid; gap:10px; margin-top:18px; }
    .brief-checklist span { display:block; padding-left:24px; color:var(--brief-muted); font-size:16px; line-height:1.4; }
    .brief-checklist span::before { content:'✓'; display:inline-block; width:24px; margin-left:-24px; color:var(--brief-copper); font-weight:800; }
    .brief-timeline { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(5,1fr); gap:10px; margin-top:34px; }
    .brief-timeline-step { padding:20px; background:#fffdf7; border-top:5px solid var(--brief-copper); }
    .brief-timeline-step strong { display:block; margin:12px 0 8px; color:var(--brief-green); font-size:18px; }
    .brief-timeline-step span { color:var(--brief-muted); font-size:14px; line-height:1.4; }
    .brief-ask { padding:76px 0 92px; background:var(--brief-green); color:#fffdf7; }
    .brief-ask h2 { max-width:760px; color:#fffdf7; }
    .brief-ask p { max-width:720px; color:#d5dfd6; font-size:20px; line-height:1.55; }
    .brief-button { display:inline-block; margin-top:18px; padding:16px 22px; background:#e19a70; color:#172019; font-weight:800; text-decoration:none; }
    .brief-disclaimer { padding:20px 0 36px; color:#68716a; font-size:12px; line-height:1.5; }
    @media (max-width:800px) { .brief-hero-grid,.brief-explainer,.brief-video-grid,.brief-money,.brief-partner { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:30px; }.brief-stats { grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; }.brief-hero-image img { height:380px; }.brief-service-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; }.brief-journey,.brief-timeline { grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; }.brief-workflow { grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; }.brief-workflow h3 { grid-column:1 / -1; } }
    @media (max-width:560px) { .brief-shell { width:min(100% - 32px,1120px); }.brief-stats,.brief-two-col,.brief-proof,.brief-built,.brief-economics,.brief-service-grid,.brief-journey,.brief-timeline,.brief-workflow { grid-template-columns:1fr; }.brief-section { padding:52px 0; }.brief-hero { padding-bottom:62px; }.brief-hero-grid { padding-top:54px; gap:34px; }.brief-hero h1 { font-size:54px; }.brief-hero-lead { font-size:17px; }.brief-hero-image img { height:340px; }.brief-stat { min-height:auto; }.brief-lockup span { font-size:9px; }.brief-money-row { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:4px; }.brief-workflow h3 { grid-column:auto; } }
  </style>

  <div class="brief-page">
    <section class="brief-hero"><div class="brief-shell"><div class="brief-hero-grid"><div><div class="brief-kicker">THE OPPORTUNITY / STATE OF STICK GOLF</div><h1>Golf already has the players, places, and passion.<br /><em>Now connect the experience.</em></h1><p class="brief-hero-lead">State of Stick Golf connects the golfer, course, clubhouse, league, and season through one familiar action: tap.</p><div class="brief-demo-note"><strong>Important:</strong> Course names, maps, and round details shown in this product are demonstration data. Cedar Ridge is not a confirmed partner or approved live pilot.</div></div><div class="brief-hero-image"><img src="/art/golf-fairway-hero.png" alt="Golf fairway with a physical connected course medallion" /><div class="brief-image-caption">A proposed physical course marker becomes a doorway to the digital experience.</div></div></div></div></section>

    <section class="brief-section"><div class="brief-shell"><div class="brief-kicker">WHY NOW / VERIFIED INDUSTRY FACTS</div><h2>This is not a small hobby market.</h2><p class="brief-intro">The market is large, active, and still changing. These numbers show why a better connection between play, courses, and communities matters.</p><div class="brief-stats"><article class="brief-stat"><strong>47.2M</strong><span>U.S. golf participants in 2024</span><small>Includes on-course and off-course participation.</small></article><article class="brief-stat"><strong>28.1M</strong><span>U.S. on-course golfers in 2024</span><small>The highest level since the Great Recession.</small></article><article class="brief-stat"><strong>500M+</strong><span>Rounds played in the U.S. in 2024</span><small>The fifth consecutive year above 500 million rounds.</small></article><article class="brief-stat"><strong>$102B</strong><span>Direct annual U.S. golf impact</span><small>The broader economic impact is $226.5B and supports 1.65M jobs.</small></article></div><p class="brief-source">Sources: <a href="https://www.ngf.org/short-game/golfs-state-of-industry-in-3-minutes/" rel="noopener">National Golf Foundation, 2024 industry overview</a>; <a href="https://rulesworkshops.usga.org/content/usga/home-page/articles/2025/03/golfs-new-narrative.html" rel="noopener">USGA, Golf’s New Narrative</a>; <a href="https://www.ngf.org/member-publication/golf-economic-impact-report-2023/" rel="noopener">NGF, 2023 Economic Impact Report</a>.</p></div></section>

    <section class="brief-section alt"><div class="brief-shell"><div class="brief-kicker">THE PROBLEM IN PLAIN ENGLISH</div><h2>Golf has places, people,<br />and activity. They are disconnected.</h2><div class="brief-two-col"><article class="brief-card"><div class="brief-number">TODAY</div><h3>The golfer carries the burden</h3><p>Scorekeeping, league details, clubhouse requests, course information, and memories are spread across different tools—or handled manually.</p></article><article class="brief-card"><div class="brief-number">THE OPENING</div><h3>Make the course easier to use</h3><p>A tap at the right physical point can show the next useful action: record a score, ask a question, contact the clubhouse, join a challenge, or see the season.</p></article></div></div></section>

    <section class="brief-section brief-services"><div class="brief-shell"><div class="brief-kicker">PROPOSED OPERATOR SERVICE LAYER</div><h2>Give golfers more reasons<br />to use the course.</h2><p class="brief-intro">The network can become a simple service doorway for a course, club, resort, or golf event. These are proposed offerings to validate with operators—not live integrations or promised capabilities today.</p><div class="brief-service-grid"><article class="brief-service-card"><div class="brief-number">01 / ON-COURSE COMMERCE</div><h3>Food and drinks, wherever the golfer is</h3><p>Let a golfer tap at a hole, cart point, or service marker to view approved menus, place a food or beverage request, and receive clear pickup or delivery instructions.</p><small>Possible revenue: order margin, service fee, or operator subscription</small></article><article class="brief-service-card"><div class="brief-number">02 / PLAYER SERVICE</div><h3>Make the round easier</h3><p>Request water, towels, rentals, pace assistance, cart help, lost-and-found support, or a clubhouse question without hunting for a phone number.</p><small>Possible value: fewer interruptions and faster staff response</small></article><article class="brief-service-card"><div class="brief-number">03 / COURSE GUIDANCE</div><h3>Put the right information at the right hole</h3><p>Offer approved hole context, local rules, amenities, accessibility information, pace reminders, and Golf Agent answers grounded in course content.</p><small>Operator-controlled content · no invented course facts</small></article><article class="brief-service-card"><div class="brief-number">04 / LEAGUES & EVENTS</div><h3>Turn play into a connected program</h3><p>Run scoring, announcements, challenges, tournament check-ins, tee-time moments, and event memories from one portable golfer experience.</p><small>Possible revenue: event programs and recurring league subscriptions</small></article><article class="brief-service-card"><div class="brief-number">05 / SPONSORS & PARTNERS</div><h3>Create measurable partner moments</h3><p>Give sponsors useful, permission-based touchpoints around a tournament, clubhouse, hole, charitable event, or seasonal challenge.</p><small>Possible revenue: activations, placements, and partner programs</small></article><article class="brief-service-card"><div class="brief-number">06 / OPERATOR INSIGHT</div><h3>See what golfers actually need</h3><p>Summarize taps, requests, recurring questions, event activity, and unmet service moments so operators can improve the experience and decide what to offer next.</p><small>Possible revenue: platform subscription and reporting services</small></article></div></div></section>

    <section class="brief-section brief-video-section"><div class="brief-shell"><div class="brief-video-grid"><div class="brief-video-copy"><div class="brief-kicker">SEE THE IDEA IN MOTION</div><h2>One tap can connect the whole experience.</h2><p>A golfer arrives, connects with the course, and gets the next useful action—from scoring and course information to clubhouse requests, leagues, events, and memories.</p><p>This is the kind of simple, physical-to-digital experience the founding golf partner would help us test and shape with real golfers and operators.</p><div class="brief-video-note"><strong>Concept video:</strong> The course, people, and details shown here are illustrative. They do not represent a live or approved course partnership.</div></div><figure class="brief-video-frame"><video controls playsinline preload="metadata" poster="/art/golf-fairway-hero.png"><source src="/video/sosgolf.mp4" type="video/mp4" />Your browser does not support the golf concept video.</video><figcaption>Illustrative product vision · State of Stick Golf</figcaption></figure></div></div></section>

    <section class="brief-section dark" id="how-it-works"><div class="brief-shell"><div class="brief-kicker">ONE GOLFER / ONE ROUND</div><h2>Make the physical course<br />feel connected.</h2><p class="brief-intro" style="color:#d4dbd4;">The technology stays in the background. The golfer sees a clear, useful response at the moment it matters.</p><div class="brief-journey"><article class="brief-journey-step"><div class="brief-number">01 / ARRIVE</div><strong>The golfer arrives</strong><span>The course welcomes a player, guest, family, or league participant.</span></article><article class="brief-journey-step"><div class="brief-number">02 / TAP</div><strong>They tap a marker</strong><span>A flagstick, tee marker, cart, clubhouse point, or passport opens the next moment.</span></article><article class="brief-journey-step"><div class="brief-number">03 / USE</div><strong>They get help</strong><span>Record a score, ask a question, see hole context, request service, or join an event.</span></article><article class="brief-journey-step"><div class="brief-number">04 / PLAY</div><strong>The round continues</strong><span>League standings, challenges, announcements, and shared memories stay connected.</span></article><article class="brief-journey-step"><div class="brief-number">05 / RETURN</div><strong>The season carries on</strong><span>The golfer passport gives the player a reason to come back and play elsewhere.</span></article></div></div></section>

    <section class="brief-section alt"><div class="brief-shell"><div class="brief-kicker">PROPOSED PILOT / WHAT WE CAN PROVE FIRST</div><h2>Start with three useful<br />workflows—not a giant rollout.</h2><p class="brief-intro">These are proposed pilot workflows. No course partnership, customer adoption, or live results are being claimed today.</p><div class="brief-workflows"><article class="brief-workflow"><div><div class="brief-number">01 / COURSE</div><h3>Make the course easier to use</h3></div><div><label>CURRENT PROBLEM</label><p>Course guidance, questions, and clubhouse requests are often disconnected from the player’s moment.</p><label style="margin-top:16px;">PROPOSED EXPERIENCE</label><p>Tap the right course point to get approved guidance, Ask the Golf Agent for grounded answers from approved course context, or request help from the clubhouse.</p></div><div><label>WHO BENEFITS</label><p>Golfers get clarity; staff get fewer interruptions and better context.</p><label style="margin-top:16px;">MEASURE</label><p>Tap use, completed requests, response time, repeat visits, and golfer feedback.</p></div></article><article class="brief-workflow"><div><div class="brief-number">02 / SEASON</div><h3>Keep a league connected</h3></div><div><label>CURRENT PROBLEM</label><p>Scores, announcements, challenges, and standings are scattered across messages, spreadsheets, and separate tools.</p><label style="margin-top:16px;">PROPOSED EXPERIENCE</label><p>Connect scoring, announcements, challenges, and a golfer passport to one portable season with operator-controlled AI guidance.</p></div><div><label>WHO BENEFITS</label><p>Players stay engaged; commissioners and operators get a clearer season.</p><label style="margin-top:16px;">MEASURE</label><p>Round completion, return play, standings engagement, disputes, and second-season interest.</p></div></article><article class="brief-workflow"><div><div class="brief-number">03 / EVENT</div><h3>Make tournaments more interactive</h3></div><div><label>CURRENT PROBLEM</label><p>Events create energy for one day, but participation and memories often disappear afterward.</p><label style="margin-top:16px;">PROPOSED EXPERIENCE</label><p>Use tap points for participation, sponsor or partner moments, updates, shared memories, and a lasting event passport.</p></div><div><label>WHO BENEFITS</label><p>Players, organizers, sponsors, charities, and courses get a more measurable event.</p><label style="margin-top:16px;">MEASURE</label><p>Participation, taps, sponsor interactions, repeat attendance, and post-event engagement.</p></div></article></div><div class="brief-proof"><figure><img src="/art/flagstick-tap-medallion.png" alt="Physical golf flagstick tap medallion concept" /><figcaption>Concept: the physical doorway.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/art/golf-emblems.png" alt="Green and copper golf passport emblem concepts" /><figcaption>Concept: the portable golf identity.</figcaption></figure></div></div></section>

    <section class="brief-section"><div class="brief-shell"><div class="brief-kicker">THE FOUNDING-PARTNER OPPORTUNITY</div><h2>Help lead the<br />golf vertical.</h2><p class="brief-intro">Your value is not writing software. Your value is knowing the game well enough to help us build the right thing, with the right people, in the right order.</p><div class="brief-partner"><article class="brief-card"><div class="brief-number">WHAT YOU WOULD DO</div><h3>Bring judgment and relationships</h3><div class="brief-checklist"><span>Help select the first proposed pilot course.</span><span>Introduce the right course and golf contacts.</span><span>Pressure-test what golfers and operators actually need.</span><span>Test the experience with a defined group of golfers.</span><span>Advise what should be built next.</span><span>Help turn the pilot into a repeatable paid offering.</span></div></article><article class="brief-card"><div class="brief-number">WHAT STATE OF STICK WOULD HANDLE</div><h3>Build and support the system</h3><div class="brief-checklist"><span>Technology, product development, and implementation.</span><span>Design, hosting, data boundaries, and technical support.</span><span>Product documentation, measurement, and iteration.</span><span>Business structure, agreements, and operational follow-through.</span><span>You would not need to fund the company or carry the business alone.</span></div></article></div><div class="brief-offer-note"><strong>The role in one sentence:</strong> you would help us decide what golf needs first and help open the right doors; State of Stick would build, operate, and support the product around that judgment.</div></div></section>
    <section class="brief-section"><div class="brief-shell"><div class="brief-kicker">WHY WE THOUGHT OF YOU</div><h2>We need practical golf judgment,<br />not another software executive.</h2><div class="brief-two-col"><article class="brief-card"><div class="brief-number">THE PERSPECTIVE</div><h3>Make the idea work in the real world</h3><p>You understand what makes people participate, what makes an operation workable, and what earns trust. Your experience around SpartanNash and the West Michigan business community gives you a practical perspective and relationship context that are more valuable here than technical vocabulary.</p></article><article class="brief-card"><div class="brief-number">THE ROLE</div><h3>Turn a concept into a business</h3><p>We are asking you to challenge our assumptions, help us find the right first relationships, and decide whether this creates enough value for a course and its golfers to pay for it.</p></article></div><div class="brief-offer-note"><strong>What we are not assuming:</strong> that you want another full-time job, that you should fund the project, or that you need to understand the software. The first conversation is simply whether the opportunity is worth testing together.</div></div></section>

    <section class="brief-section alt"><div class="brief-shell"><div class="brief-kicker">A MANAGEABLE FIRST COMMITMENT</div><h2>Start with six months,<br />then decide together.</h2><p class="brief-intro">A defined pilot partnership creates a serious test without creating an indefinite obligation.</p><div class="brief-timeline"><article class="brief-timeline-step"><div class="brief-number">MONTH 01</div><strong>Choose the direction</strong><span>Select the proposed pilot course, workflow, and success measures.</span></article><article class="brief-timeline-step"><div class="brief-number">MONTH 02</div><strong>Open the doors</strong><span>Introduce the right course, event, and golfer relationships.</span></article><article class="brief-timeline-step"><div class="brief-number">MONTHS 03–04</div><strong>Test the experience</strong><span>Run one proposed workflow with a defined group and document feedback.</span></article><article class="brief-timeline-step"><div class="brief-number">MONTH 05</div><strong>Measure the proof</strong><span>Review use, repeat interest, operational value, and what needs changing.</span></article><article class="brief-timeline-step"><div class="brief-number">MONTH 06</div><strong>Choose the next step</strong><span>Pursue paid continuation, revise the offer, or stop with a clear result.</span></article></div></div></section>

    <section class="brief-section"><div class="brief-shell"><div class="brief-kicker">THE PRODUCT OWNER OPPORTUNITY</div><h2>How could you make money<br />helping build this?</h2><p class="brief-intro">The product owner is not being asked to invest. The role is to help turn the product into a useful, paid golf business—and participate in the revenue or ownership created by that work.</p><div class="brief-money"><article class="brief-card"><div class="brief-number">PATH 01 / PAID BUILDER</div><h3>Earn while you operate the pilot</h3><p>A part-time product-owner agreement can include a modest monthly fee, clear milestones, and a revenue share on the courses, events, and programs he directly helps launch.</p><div class="brief-money-list"><div class="brief-money-row"><strong>Monthly fee</strong><span>Compensation for regular product decisions, meetings, testing, and operator relationships.</span></div><div class="brief-money-row"><strong>Milestones</strong><span>Bonuses when the pilot reaches agreed proof points, such as its first paid continuation or course agreement.</span></div><div class="brief-money-row"><strong>Revenue share</strong><span>A defined percentage of net golf revenue from accounts he originates or helps launch, for a fixed period.</span></div></div></article><article class="brief-card"><div class="brief-number">PATH 02 / FOUNDING PARTNER</div><h3>Trade some cash for more upside</h3><p>If he wants a deeper role, a separate written agreement could combine a smaller fee with a larger success-based share or a modest vesting equity grant in the golf venture.</p><div class="brief-money-list"><div class="brief-money-row"><strong>More upside</strong><span>Participation grows if the golf vertical becomes a meaningful business.</span></div><div class="brief-money-row"><strong>Vesting</strong><span>Ownership should vest over time and depend on defined contribution, not be granted all at once.</span></div><div class="brief-money-row"><strong>No obligation</strong><span>Investment remains optional and should be documented separately from the work agreement.</span></div></div></article></div><div class="brief-economics"><article class="brief-stat"><strong>$60K</strong><span>Illustrative annual course revenue</span><small>10 courses × $500/month = $60,000 before costs. Example only.</small></article><article class="brief-stat"><strong>$150K</strong><span>Illustrative annual course revenue</span><small>25 courses × $500/month = $150,000 before costs. Example only.</small></article><article class="brief-stat"><strong>$600K</strong><span>Illustrative annual course revenue</span><small>100 courses × $500/month = $600,000 before costs. Example only.</small></article></div><div class="brief-offer-note"><strong>Possible revenue sources:</strong> course platform subscriptions, pilot and implementation fees, event and tournament programs, sponsor or partner activations, reporting and analytics, and golf-specific services.</div></div></section>

    <section class="brief-ask" id="founding-partnership"><div class="brief-shell"><div class="brief-kicker">THE INVITATION</div><h2>Help create the value.<br />Share in the value.</h2><p>You already understand golfers, golf courses, and what makes people come back. We are asking whether you would like to help shape this vertical from the beginning.</p><p>You would help create the value—and share in the value created. The first step is a conversation about the founding partnership, not an investment decision and not a commitment to an unapproved course.</p><a class="brief-button" href="#founding-partnership">Discuss the founding partnership →</a></div></section>
